From 18f68de2e60612afa66faef96bea370e32924da8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:54:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] tla: validate restarts at the BecomeFollower after
 loading state

newRaft logs InitState before loadState, so on a restart the InitState
line shows the state before the persisted state is loaded: term 0, an
empty config, and the snapshot's commit index rather than the persisted
one. RestartIfLogged validated the restarted state against that line, so
no trace with a restart could validate.

Don't validate at InitState. Instead, check the restored state at the
BecomeFollower that newRaft logs after loading it. That line is
recognized as the one whose previous line for the node, apart from the
ApplyConfChange lines that restoring the config logs, is the InitState.

An alternative is to log InitState after loadState in raft.go; this
keeps the trace format unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tla/Traceetcdraft.tla | 31 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tla/Traceetcdraft.tla b/tla/Traceetcdraft.tla
index ccbae2d..cc46cf1 100644
--- a/tla/Traceetcdraft.tla
+++ b/tla/Traceetcdraft.tla
@@ -358,10 +358,37 @@ ReadyIfLogged(i) ==
     /\ LoglineIsNodeEvent("Ready", i)
     /\ Ready(i)
 
+\* raft.go newRaft logs InitState before loadState, so on a restart the
+\* InitState line shows the state before the persisted state is loaded (the
+\* snapshot's commit index, term 0, an empty config), which the restored
+\* state does not match. The restart is therefore not validated at
+\* InitState; the restored state is checked at the BecomeFollower line that
+\* newRaft logs after loading it (RestartBecomeFollowerIfLogged).
 RestartIfLogged(i) ==
     /\ LoglineIsNodeEvent("InitState", i)
     /\ Restart(i)
-    /\ ValidatePostStates(i)
+
+\* The last line for node i before the current one, ignoring the
+\* ApplyConfChange lines that restoring the config logs.
+PrevNodeLineIgnoringConfChange(i) ==
+    LET k == SelectLastInSubSeq(TraceLog, 1, l-1,
+                 LAMBDA x: x.event.nid = i /\ x.event.name # "ApplyConfChange")
+    IN IF k > 0 THEN TraceLog[k] ELSE logline
+
+\* The BecomeFollower that newRaft logs right after a restart: the previous
+\* line for node i, apart from restored-config ApplyConfChange lines, is the
+\* InitState that RestartIfLogged consumed. Restart already restored the
+\* state; check that it matches.
+RestartBecomeFollowerIfLogged(i) ==
+    /\ LoglineIsNodeEvent("BecomeFollower", i)
+    /\ PrevNodeLineIgnoringConfChange(i).event.name = "InitState"
+    /\ state[i] = Follower
+    /\ currentTerm[i] = logline.event.state.term
+    /\ votedFor[i] = logline.event.state.vote
+    /\ Len(log[i]) = logline.event.log
+    /\ commitIndex[i] = logline.event.state.commit
+    /\ config[i].jointConfig = ConfFromLog(logline)
+    /\ UNCHANGED <<vars>>
 
 LoglineIsBecomeFollowerInUpdateTermOrReturnToFollower ==
     /\ LoglineIsEvent("BecomeFollower")
@@ -426,6 +453,8 @@ TraceNextNonReceiveActions ==
           /\ \E i \in Server: RestartIfLogged(i)
        \/ /\ LoglineIsEvent("BecomeFollower")
           /\ \E i \in Server: StepDownToFollowerIfLogged(i)
+       \/ /\ LoglineIsEvent("BecomeFollower")
+          /\ \E i \in Server: RestartBecomeFollowerIfLogged(i)
        \/ SkipUnusedLogline
     /\ StepToNextTrace
     
